---
import LegalLayout from '../../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
---

<LegalLayout
  lang="en"
  title="Terms & Conditions - Cheflink"
  description="Terms and Conditions of use for Cheflink, the QR ordering and table tab management platform."
  canonicalPath="/en/terms/"
>
  <main class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-10 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 lg:py-12">
    <article class="rounded-3xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6 shadow-sm sm:p-8">
      <header class="mb-6 border-b border-slate-100 pb-4">
        <h1 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl">Terms & Conditions</h1>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-600">Last updated: January 2025</p>
      </header>

      <section class="mt-6 space-y-2">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900">1. Introduction</h2>
        <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-700">Welcome to <strong>Cheflink</strong> ("the Platform"). These Terms and Conditions govern use of the Platform by restaurants, bars, cafés, and other food and beverage establishments (hereinafter "Venue" or "Professional User"), as well as by end guests who place orders via QR codes (hereinafter "Guests").</p>
        <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-700">By accessing or using Cheflink, you agree to be bound by these Terms and Conditions.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-6 space-y-2">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900">2. Definitions</h2>
        <ul class="list-disc space-y-1 pl-5 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-700">
          <li><strong>Platform:</strong> the Cheflink software (including the web interface, admin panel, and QR ordering pages).</li>
          <li><strong>Venue / Professional User:</strong> a business that uses Cheflink to receive orders and manage table tabs.</li>
          <li><strong>Guest:</strong> a person who places orders via QR codes generated by the Venue using Cheflink.</li>
          <li><strong>Account:</strong> a profile or access credential assigned to a Venue or its authorized staff.</li>
          <li><strong>Services:</strong> all features offered by Cheflink.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-6 space-y-2">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900">3. Scope of Service</h2>
        <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-700">Cheflink provides a technology tool for Venues to manage QR orders, table tabs, and kitchen order flow. Cheflink:</p>
        <ul class="mt-1 list-disc space-y-1 pl-5 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-700">
          <li>Does not sell, prepare, or deliver food or beverages.</li>
          <li>Is not a party to the commercial relationship between the Venue and the Guest.</li>
          <li>Does not set prices or sales terms for products offered by the Venue.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-6 space-y-2">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900">4. Accounts and Access</h2>
        <ul class="list-disc space-y-1 pl-5 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-700">
          <li>To use the Platform as a Venue, you must create an account with accurate, complete, and current information.</li>
          <li>You are responsible for maintaining the confidentiality of your credentials.</li>
          <li>The Venue is responsible for managing access for authorized staff and revoking access when appropriate.</li>
          <li>Cheflink may suspend or cancel access in cases of misuse or violation of these Terms.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-6 space-y-2">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900">5. Acceptable Use</h2>
        <ul class="mt-1 list-disc space-y-1 pl-5 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-700">
          <li>Use the Platform in accordance with applicable law and these Terms.</li>
          <li>Do not attempt unauthorized access to systems, accounts, or data belonging to others.</li>
          <li>Do not alter, copy, distribute, or reverse-engineer Cheflink's software without express permission.</li>
          <li>Do not use Cheflink for illegal or fraudulent activities.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-6 space-y-2">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900">6. Venue Responsibilities</h2>
        <ul class="list-disc space-y-1 pl-5 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-700">
          <li>Correctly configure the menu, prices, service charges, taxes, and any discounts.</li>
          <li>Review and fulfill orders received through the Platform in a timely manner.</li>
          <li>Clearly inform Guests about any special conditions.</li>
          <li>Comply with local regulations on consumer protection, food safety, and data privacy.</li>
          <li>Verify that tab calculations and additional charges are correct before charging the Guest.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-6 space-y-2">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900">7. Pricing, Plans, and Payments</h2>
        <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-700">Cheflink may offer free and paid plans for Venues. Unless otherwise stated:</p>
        <ul class="mt-1 list-disc space-y-1 pl-5 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-700">
          <li>Prices may be expressed in the Venue's local currency or another agreed currency.</li>
          <li>Charges are billed per period and are non-refundable once the period has begun.</li>
          <li>We may update prices in the future with reasonable advance notice to the Venue.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-6 space-y-2">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900">8. Intellectual Property</h2>
        <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-700">Cheflink, including its source code, design, interfaces, and brand, is the property of the Platform owner or its licensors and is protected by intellectual property laws.</p>
        <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-700">The Venue retains all rights to its own content (e.g., restaurant name, logos, dish photos, menu descriptions) and grants us a limited license to display that content within the Platform while the service is active.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-6 space-y-2">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900">9. Privacy and Data Protection</h2>
        <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-700">The processing of personal data for Guests and Venues is governed by our <strong>Privacy Policy</strong>, which forms part of these Terms. The Venue agrees to use Guest data only for purposes related to order management and business operations.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-6 space-y-2">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900">10. Availability, Maintenance, and Changes</h2>
        <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-700">Cheflink strives to keep the Platform continuously available but does not guarantee the absence of temporary interruptions due to maintenance, updates, or technical issues.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-6 space-y-2">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900">11. Limitation of Liability</h2>
        <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-700">To the extent permitted by applicable law, Cheflink is not liable for:</p>
        <ul class="mt-1 list-disc space-y-1 pl-5 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-700">
          <li>Losses arising from errors in the Venue's price, menu, or charge configuration.</li>
          <li>Guest claims related to product quality, delivery times, or billing errors.</li>
          <li>Indirect, incidental, special, or consequential damages.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-6 space-y-2">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900">12. Changes to These Terms</h2>
        <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-700">We may update these Terms from time to time. Continued use of Cheflink after the effective date of any changes constitutes acceptance of the updated Terms.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-6 space-y-2">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900">13. Governing Law and Jurisdiction</h2>
        <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-700">These Terms are governed by the laws of <em>[indicate your country or jurisdiction]</em>. Any disputes shall be submitted to the competent courts of <em>[city / country]</em>.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-6 space-y-2">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900">14. Contact</h2>
        <ul class="mt-1 list-none space-y-1 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-700">
          <li><strong>Email:</strong> <a href="mailto:support@cheflink.com" class="text-orange-600 hover:underline">support@cheflink.com</a></li>
          <li><strong>Suggested subject:</strong> "Cheflink Terms & Conditions Inquiry"</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <p class="mt-8 border-t border-slate-100 pt-4 text-center text-xs text-slate-500">
        This text is a reference example. Adjust, translate, or expand it to meet the legal requirements of your business.
      </p>
    </article>
  </main>
</LegalLayout>
